    {
      "cve": "CVE-2026-82253",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-82253"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "gitoxide (Rust crates gix \u003c= 0.72.0 and gix-validate \u003c= 0.10.0) contains a path traversal vulnerability. The submodule name validation function in gix-validate only checks the first occurrence of '..' via name.find(b\"..\"), allowing crafted names such as 'a..b/../../../.git/' to bypass the check; additionally this validation is never invoked in production code paths. Combined with a trust inheritance flaw in Submodule::open(), where the parent repository's git_dir_trust (Trust::Full) is cloned and the ownership verification is skipped, an attacker can craft a malicious .gitmodules file so that a victim tool built on gitoxide reads arbitrary git repository configuration (including embedded credentials) with full trust, bypassing safe-directory protections. Fixed in gix 0.82.0 and gix-validate 0.11.1.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
      "product_status": {
        "recommended": [
          "openSUSE Tumbleweed:cargo-c-0:0.10.25-1.1.aarch64",
          "openSUSE Tumbleweed:cargo-c-0:0.10.25-1.1.ppc64le",
